would be his Hebrew home-name.","verses":179,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"timotheus_2863","name":"Timotheus","also":"Timothy","summary":"Honouring God, a young disciple who was Paul’s companion in many of his journeyings. His mother, Eunice, and his grandmother, Lois, are mentioned as eminent for their piety (2 Tim. 1:5).","verses":24,"father":"","mother":"Eunice","v":[1,19]},{"id":"silas_2740","name":"Silas","also":"Silvanus","summary":"Wood, a prominent member of the church at Jerusalem; also called Silvanus. He and Judas, surnamed Barsabas, were chosen by the church there to accompany Paul and Barnabas on their return to Antioch from the council of the apostles and elders (Acts 15:22), as bearers of the decree adopted by the council.","verses":17,"father":"","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"holy_spirit_7400","name":"Holy Spirit","also":"Comforter, Holy Ghost","summary":"The third Person of the adorable Trinity.","verses":246,"father":"","mother":"","v":[22]}],"places":[{"id":"achaia_16","name":"Achaia","kind":"Region","lat":37.5,"lon":22.5,"summary":"The name originally of a narrow strip of territory in Greece, on the north-west of the Peloponnesus. Subsequently it was applied by the Romans to the whole Peloponnesus, now called the Morea, and the south of Greece.","verses":10,"v":[1]},{"id":"corinth_306","name":"Corinth","kind":"City","lat":37.90604,"lon":22.87872,"summary":"A Grecian city, on the isthmus which joins the Peloponnesus to the mainland of Greece. It is about 48 miles west of Athens. The ancient city was destroyed by the Romans (B.C. 146), and that mentioned in the New Testament was quite a new city, having been rebuilt about a century afterwards and peopled by a colony of freedmen from Rome.","verses":6,"v":[1,23]},{"id":"asia_108","name":"Asia","kind":"Region","lat":39.64015,"lon":31.03325,"summary":"Is used to denote Proconsular Asia, a Roman province which embraced the western parts of Asia Minor, and of which Ephesus was the capital, in Acts 2:9; 6:9; 16:6; 19:10, 22; 20:4, 16, 18, etc., and probably Asia Minor in Acts 19:26, 27; 21:27; 24:18; 27:2.","verses":18,"v":[8]},{"id":"judea_657","name":"Judea","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"After the Captivity this name was applied to the whole of the country west of the Jordan (Hag. 1:1, 14; 2:2).","verses":44,"v":[16]},{"id":"macedonia_747","name":"Macedonia","kind":"Region","lat":40.73292,"lon":22.9352,"summary":"In New Testament times, was a Roman province lying north of Greece. It was governed by a propraetor with the title of proconsul. Paul was summoned by the vision of the “man of Macedonia” to preach the gospel there (Acts 16:9).","verses":21,"v":[16]}],"events":[],"traditions":[["oaths-and-swearing",23,23]],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3972,652,652,5547,5547,2424,1223,2307,2307,2316,2316,2532,5095,3588,80,3588,3588,1577,2316,2316,1722,2882,4862,4862,3956,3588,40,1510,882],[5485,2532,1515,4771,4771,575,2316,1473,3962,2532,2962,2962,2424,5547],[2128,2128,3588,2316,2532,3962,1473,1473,2962,2424,5547,3588,3962,3628,3628,2532,2316,2316,3956,3956,3874],[3588,3870,1473,1909,3956,1473,2347,1519,1519,1473,1410,3870,3588,1722,3956,2347,1223,3588,3874,846,846,3870,3870,5259,2316],[3754,2531,2531,3588,3804,5547,5547,4052,1519,1473,3779,2532,1223,5547,1473,3874,4052],[1535,2346,2346,2346,5228,5228,5228,4771,3874,2532,4991,1535,3870,3870,3870,5228,5228,5228,4771,3874,3588,1754,1722,1722,5281,5281,3588,3588,846,3804,1473,3958],[2532,1473,1680,5228,4771,949,949,1492,1492,1492,3754,5613,5613,2844,2844,3588,3588,3804,3779,2532,2532,2532,2532,3588,3588,3874],[2309,2309,2309,2309,4771,50,50,50,80,5228,3588,2347,1473,1096,1722,773,773,773,773,916,916,916,916,916,5236,5236,1411,1411,1411,1411,5620,5620,1473,1820,2532,3588,2198],[235,846,2192,1438,1438,1438,3588,610,2288,2288,2443,2443,2443,1510,1510,1510,3982,1909,1438,235,1909,2316,3588,1453,3588,3498],[3739,4506,4506,1473,1537,5082,5082,5082,5082,2532,4506,4506